frame: bound spline control points and their deltas as libjxl does (ValidateSplinePointPos:
coordinates and accumulated deltas below 2^23 in magnitude, delta-deltas below 2^30). Splines are
rendered in f32, and at coordinates around 2^24 and above a step of one unit along the spline no
longer changes the position, so Spline::get_samples never reached the end of a segment and grew its
list of arcs without bound: "capacity overflow" on 32-bit targets, unbounded memory use and a hang
on 64-bit ones. The parse-time checks of fix-spline-point-count-overflow bound the number of
points, not their positions, so they don't catch this; this patch goes after it in the same
function. Test: spline_position_bounds (crates/jxl-oxide-tests/tests/spline_position_bounds.rs);
without the fix it fails with "capacity overflow" on i686 and does not finish on x86_64.

Upstream: not reported; the code is unchanged at upstream HEAD (c0cc4c7, 2026-08-15).

